# text = Others , men and women , dipped in the puddles with little mugs of mutilated earthenware , or even with handkerchiefs from women's heads , which were squeezed dry into infants' mouths ; others made small mud - embankments , to stem the wine as it ran ; others , directed by lookers-on up at high windows , darted here and there , to cut off little streams of wine that started away in new directions ; others devoted themselves to the sodden and lee-dyed pieces of the cask , licking , and even champing the moister wine-rotted fragments with eager relish .
