# text = After bursting open a door of idiotic obstinacy with a weak rattle in its throat , you fell into Tellson's down two steps , and came to your senses in a miserable little shop , with two little counters , where the oldest of men made your cheque shake as if the wind rustled it , while they examined the signature by the dingiest of windows , which were always under a shower-bath of mud from Fleet-street , and which were made the dingier by their own iron bars proper , and the heavy shadow of Temple Bar .
