# text = Stryver , massing his papers before him , whispered with those who sat near , and from time to time glanced anxiously at the jury ; while all the spectators moved more or less , and grouped themselves anew ; while even my Lord himself arose from his seat , and slowly paced up and down his platform , not unattended by a suspicion in the minds of the audience that his state was feverish ; this one man sat leaning back , with his torn gown half off him , his untidy wig put on just as it had happened to fight on his head after its removal , his hands in his pockets , and his eyes on the ceiling as they had been all day .
