# text = Citizen Gabelle hinted , with infinite delicacy and politeness , that in the pressure of business imposed on the Tribunal by the multitude of enemies of the Republic with which it had to deal , he had been slightly overlooked in his prison of the Abbaye -- in fact , had rather passed out of the Tribunal's patriotic remembrance -- until three days ago ; when he had been summoned before it , and had been set at liberty on the Jury's declaring themselves satisfied that the accusation against him was answered , as to himself , by the surrender of the citizen Evremonde , called Darnay .
