# text = She and Jerry had beheld the coach start , had known who it was that Solomon brought , had passed some ten minutes in tortures of suspense , and were now concluding their arrangements to follow the coach , even as Madame Defarge , taking her way through the streets , now drew nearer and nearer to the else-deserted lodging in which they held their consultation said Miss Pross , whose agitation was so great that she could hardly speak , or stand , or move , or live returned Mr . Cruncher said Miss Pross , wildly crying returned Mr . Cruncher cried Miss Pross , still wildly crying said Mr . Cruncher , who was all in a tremble , and who spoke with an ashy and solemn visage returned Miss Pross returned Jerry said Miss Pross , striving to dry her eyes and compose herself proceeded Mr . Cruncher , with a most alarming tendency to hold forth as from a pulpit cried the distracted Miss Pross proceeded Mr . Cruncher , with additional solemnity , additional slowness , and additional tendency to hold forth and hold out This was Mr . Cruncher's conclusion after a protracted but vain endeavour to find a better one .
